{
 "id": "01a1065a-59a1-73c1-bad1-e108f9f228f7",
 "content": "scripts/export.py produces the monthly invoice report that Finance imports into their accounting tool at the start of each month. It runs from the ops cron on the 2nd at 06:00 UTC and writes one file per environment to EXPORT_BUCKET under `exports/<YYYY-MM>/invoices.csv`. Finance reconciles the totals against the ledger, so every finalized invoice of the month must appear exactly once, including zero-amount ones; drafts are excluded. Columns, in order: invoice id, customer id, subtotal, tax, total, finalized date. Amounts are integer cents with no currency symbol. Format (Finance moved to a new accounting tool in late Sept/Oct 2026): plain comma-separated (`,`) and dates as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`. UTF-8 without a BOM. (Previously the old tool required `;` and `DD.MM.YYYY`.)",
 "premise": "while Finance uses the new accounting tool that wants comma-separated files with ISO dates"
}
